.TH qsh-setup-host 1  "host 0.5.8" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-setup\-host \- This machine runs `qsh serve` (`\-\-peer`) or `qsh serve \-\-to` (`\-\-to` with `\-\-address`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh setup host\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-peer\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR] [\fB\-\-address\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-peer\-cert\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-forward\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR] [\fB\-\-install\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-service\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-install\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-peer\-role\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
This machine runs `qsh serve` (`\-\-peer`) or `qsh serve \-\-to` (`\-\-to` with `\-\-address`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-peer\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
The peer\*(Aqs trust\-store name; also the `device:<name>` principal of the printed `[[acl]]` rows
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<ALIAS>\fR
Serve one reverse\-listener alias instead (`qsh serve \-\-to`)
.TP
\fB\-\-address\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR
`host:port` recorded on the pin (with `\-\-to`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-\-peer\-cert\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Pin the peer from its certificate file (`\-` reads standard input) instead of minting an invite
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-forward\fR
Also require `forward.local` in the printed `[[acl]]` rows
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR
Never run ssh on this command\*(Aqs behalf: no automatic bootstrap of an unknown name, and no restarting of a pinned host\*(Aqs serve over ssh when the connection fails (`docs/CLI.md` §7). `qsh pair ssh` is not affected; it is ssh by definition
.TP
\fB\-\-install\-remote\fR
When the ssh bootstrap finds no `qsh` on the remote host (or one too old to answer it), install this machine\*(Aqs release into `~/.local/bin` there without asking (`docs/CLI.md` §7). Works with `\-\-json`
.TP
\fB\-\-service\fR
Also write the service unit file
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-install\-remote\fR
Never install or upgrade `qsh` on the remote host, and do not ask; a missing `qsh` ends as `remote_qsh_missing`
.TP
\fB\-\-peer\-role\fR \fI<ROLE>\fR
Trust role of the pin (or invite) this run writes: one of `full`, `exec`, `tunnel`, `read\-only`, `reverse`, `none` (default `full`; `none` prints `[[acl]]` rows instead, `docs/CLI.md` §6.20, ADR\-0045)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.5.8
